\label{def:groupaction}
For any subgroup $\Gamma$ of $\operatorname{SL}_2({\mathbb R})$ and for any left $\Gamma$-invariant subset $\mathcal{M} \subseteq \operatorname{GL}_2({\mathbb R})$ we define the set of $\Gamma$-automorphic functions on $\mathcal{M}$ by
\begin{align*} 
    \mathcal{A}(\Gamma \backslash \mathcal{M}):= \{\alpha:\mathcal{M} \to {\mathbb C}: \, l_\gamma \alpha = \alpha \,\, \text{for all} \,\, \gamma \in \Gamma\}.
\end{align*}

